<h1>Brownies with Chocolate Oat Frosting</h1>
<h2>Ingredients</h2>
<ul>
<li>1 cup all-purpose flour</li>
<li>1/4 cup unsweetened cocoa powder</li>
<li>2 tablespoons ground flaxseed</li>
<li>3 tablespoons brewer's yeast</li>
<li>1/2 teaspoon baking powder</li>
<li>1/4 teaspoon salt</li>
<li>1/2 cup melted coconut oil or butter</li>
<li>3/4 cup brown sugar (or coconut sugar)</li>
<li>1/4 cup honey or maple syrup</li>
<li>2 large eggs</li>
<li>2 teaspoons vanilla extract</li>
<li>2 tablespoons milk</li>
<li>1/2 cup rolled oats, finely ground in a blender or food processor</li>
<li>3/4 cup dark chocolate chips</li>
</ul>
<h2>Steps</h2>
<ol>
<li>Preheat oven to 350 degrees F. Line an 8x8-inch pan with parchment paper.</li>
<li>In a medium bowl, whisk together flour, cocoa powder, flaxseed, brewer's yeast, baking powder, and salt.</li>
<li>In a large bowl, whisk melted coconut oil or butter, sugar, honey, eggs, vanilla, and milk until smooth.</li>
<li>Add dry ingredients to wet and mix just until combined.</li>
<li>Fold in ground oats and dark chocolate chips.</li>
<li>Pour into the pan and spread evenly.</li>
<li>Bake for 22-26 minutes, until a toothpick comes out mostly clean (fudgy is good).</li>
<li>Cool completely before frosting.</li>
</ol>
<h1>Chocolate Oat Frosting</h1>
<h2>Ingredients</h2>
<ul>
<li>3 tablespoons butter, softened</li>
<li>2 tablespoons cocoa powder</li>
<li>1 cup powdered sugar</li>
<li>1/2 teaspoon vanilla extract</li>
<li>1 tablespoon milk, plus more as needed</li>
<li>1 tablespoon oat flour or finely ground oats</li>
</ul>
<h2>Steps</h2>
<ol>
<li>Beat butter until creamy.</li>
<li>Add cocoa powder, powdered sugar, and vanilla, and mix until combined.</li>
<li>Add milk and combine. Add more milk 1 teaspoon at a time until frosting is smooth and spreadable.</li>
<li>Mix in oat flour.</li>
<li>Spread over cooled brownies and refrigerate 15 minutes to set.</li>
</ol>
